055 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059055 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "031f3906-2842-53f5-8744-c69b88c3d6f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059056 #edb/ref 1080 "{6, 15}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059056 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059056 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a3e5261-c767-5ea4-90c7-133e95806277" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059057 #edb/ref 1080 "{3, 12, 24}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059057 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059057 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31ccf371-1e80-530b-800f-e238e3e44d32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059615 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7008" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059615 #edb/ref 1071 "If $X = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\},$ which of the following collections of subsets of $X$ are partitions of $X?$\n\n- $\\{ a, b, \\{ c,d,e \\}, \\{ f,g \\} \\}$\n\n- $\\{ \\{ a, b, c \\}, \\{ d,e,f \\}, \\{ g \\} \\}$\n\n- $\\{ \\emptyset, \\{ a,b,c \\}, \\{ f,g \\} \\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e647031-a93a-54b7-8b39-c6d3779a48ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059615 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each collection of subsets.\n\n- Collection I is *not* a partition because $a$ and $b$ are not subsets.\n\n- Collection II is a partition. All the subsets are non-empty, and every element of $X$ is contained in exactly one subset.\n\n- Collection III is *not* a partition. The subset $\\emptyset$ is empty, and the elements $d$ and $e$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059616 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059616 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $X = \\{ -4, -1, 2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17 \\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n\\{ \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\}, \\{ -4, 11 \\}, \\{ 14 \\}, \\, \\_\\_\\_\\_ \\, \\}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059616 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fcf768ea-80dc-5238-9694-883204f8f1f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059616 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nIn order to find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $-4 \\in \\{ -4, 11 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $-1 \\in \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $2$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- $5 \\in \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $8 \\in \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $11 \\in \\{ -4, 11 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $14 \\in \\{ 14 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $17$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\nThe elements $2$ and $17$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{ 2,17 \\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059617 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059617 #edb/ref 1071 "If $X = \\{ 5, 10, 15, \\ldots, 50 \\},$ which of the following collections of subsets of $X$ are partitions of $X?$\n\n- $\\{ \\{ 5, 10 \\}, \\{ 15, 20, 25, \\ldots, 45 \\}, \\{ 50 \\} \\}$\n\n- $\\{ \\{ 5, 10, 15, \\ldots, 30 \\}, \\{ 40, 45, 50 \\} \\}$\n\n- $\\{ \\{ 5, 10, 15, \\ldots, 50 \\} \\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059617 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0696e3c-de10-5b18-ba67-1d381ddbe0be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059617 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each collection of subsets.\n\n- Collection I is a partition. All the subsets are non-empty, and every element of $X$ is contained in exactly one subset.\n\n- Collection II is *not* a partition because the element $35$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- Collection III is a partition. There is only one subset, but that is okay. The subset is non-empty, and every element of $X$ is contained in this subset.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186371513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186378292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186378538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186397815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186417777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059615 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059812 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1b082a95-4d6e-512f-a6ed-9100498d17c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059813 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059813 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186371506 #edb/ref 175