y subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $3$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $6\\in {6,12,18}\\,✓$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $12\\in {6,12,18}\\,✓$\n\n- $15\\in {15,21}\\,✓$\n\n- $18\\in {6,12,18}\\,✓$\n\n- $21\\in {15,21}\\,✓$\n\n- $24$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $3,$ $9,$ and $24$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${3,9,24}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060748 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060748 #edb/ref 1061 25815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060748 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f50a4e80-5c54-5d58-ab17-5ed548aaeb19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060748 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060749 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060749 #edb/ref 1061 25821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060749 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6858b45d-f4c4-5f63-aed8-bbb4bb3ce478" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060749 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060750 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060750 #edb/ref 1061 25822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060750 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23b02b10-a468-528d-9a2e-4a1fa212b764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060750 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059813 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060751 #edb/ref 1061 25823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060751 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4ec4ab5b-df32-5ad9-bf35-f66b2266e9aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060751 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060958 #edb/ref 1064 "A **partition** of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset.\n\nIn other words, none of the subsets can be the null set $(\\emptyset),$ and every element of $A$ must be contained in one *and only one* subset.\n\nFor example, the following collections of subsets of $X=\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$ are all partitions:\n\n- $X_1 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2\\}, \\{ 3, 4 \\}, \\{5\\} \\}$\n- $X_2 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$\n- $X_3 = \\{ \\{ 1, 3\\}, \\{ 2\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$\n- $X_4 = \\{ \\{ 1, 4, 5\\}, \\{ 2, 3\\} \\}$\n- $X_5 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2, 3, 4\\}, \\{5\\} \\}$\n\nHowever, the following collections are *not* partitions:\n\n- $X_6 = \\{ \\{ 1\\}, \\{ 3, 4 \\}, \\{5\\} \\}$ - the number $2$ is not included in any subset\n- $X_7 = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{ 1, 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$ - includes $\\emptyset$\n- $X_8 = \\{ \\{ 1, 3\\}, \\{ 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$ - the number $3$ is included in two different subsets\n- $X_9 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2 \\}, \\{ 2, 3\\} \\}$ - missing $4$ and $5,$ and $2$ is included in two different subsets\n- $X_{10} = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 \\}$ - this not a collection of subsets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060958 #edb/ref 1065 4252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060958 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7c175282-8683-5a55-a872-02bbd19be4f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060958 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371506 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371506 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105868" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371506 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371506 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the set $X={0,1,2,3,…,10}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n{{2,3,5,7},{0,1},\\,{4,8},\\,____\\,}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371506 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc1a812c-1051-5f8d-9b27-1018f3b5ca90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371506 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $0\\in {0,1}\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\in {0,1}\\,✓$\n\n- $2\\in {2,3,5,7}\\,✓$\n\n- $3\\in {2,3,5,7}\\,✓$\n\n- $4\\in {4,8}\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\in {2,3,5,7}\\,✓$\n\n- $6$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $7\\in {2,3,5,7}$\n\n- $8\\in {4,8}\\,✓$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $10$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $6,9,$ and $10$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is ${6,9,10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371507 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "63bac6c5-dd87-541d-a9ea-3996685c77b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371508 #edb/ref 1080 "{9,10}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371508 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371508 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "970565a3-899b-5282-a25a-50e6ef102f58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371509 #edb/ref 1080 "{6,9,10}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371509 #edb/ref 10